Remove PTMIN=3 clamp for Z/W+jet processes

Line 575 unconditionally clamps PTMIN to a minimum of 3 GeV. This protects
divergent processes like PPJJ (1/pT^4 singularity at low pT-hat), but is
unnecessary for Z/W+jet processes where the Z/W mass regulates the cross
section. The clamp silently overrode PTMIN=0 configs to PTMIN=3, excluding
all events with pT-hat < 3 GeV and cutting into the low Z pT spectrum.

The fix makes the clamp conditional: Z/W+jet processes (PPZJ, PPZQ, PPZG,
PPWJ, PPWQ, PPWG) are exempt; all other processes retain the 3 GeV floor.

Verification (1000 events, pp vacuum 8160 GeV, PTMIN=0, WEXPO=1.4):
  Before fix:  PTMIN clamped to 3.0, splittings=1.83
  After fix:   PTMIN=0.0, splittings=1.83, 0 discarded events

@@ -573,7 +573,11 @@
 	if (ptmax.lt.ptmin) ptmax=sqrts
-	if (ptmin.lt.3.d0) ptmin = 3.d0
+	if ((collider.ne.'PPZJ').and.(collider.ne.'PPZQ')
+     &	  .and.(collider.ne.'PPZG').and.(collider.ne.'PPWJ')
+     &	  .and.(collider.ne.'PPWQ').and.(collider.ne.'PPWG')) then
+	  if (ptmin.lt.3.d0) ptmin = 3.d0
+	endif

