Fix PICKVTX vertex sampling bug in Ncoll-histogram mode (medium-2D.f)

The PICKVTX subroutine samples the hard-scattering vertex position from
the Ncoll histogram. In the Ncoll-histogram branch, it indexed ncollNZ
using rndIndex = int(pyr(0) * ncollSum), which has two bugs:

  1. rndIndex ranges from 0 to ncollSum-1. Index 0 is out of bounds for
     Fortran 1-based arrays — always triggers for single-collision events.
  2. ncollSum (total binary collisions) is typically larger than nzc-1
     (count of non-zero cells in ncollNZ). When rndIndex >= nzc, the code
     accesses zero-initialized memory, placing the vertex at (0,0) — the
     fireball center — for 5-27% of events per hydro profile.

READNCOLL already builds ncollpDist(1:ncollSum, 1:2) — one row per
binary collision, with cells duplicated proportionally to their Ncoll
count — but this array was never referenced (dead code). The fix
switches PICKVTX to use ncollpDist with correct 1-based indexing.

--- jewel-2.4.0-2D/medium-2D.f
+++ jewel-2.4.0-2D-MOD/medium-2D.f
@@ -421,1 +421,1 @@
-         rndIndex = int(pyr(0) * ncollSum)
+         rndIndex = int(pyr(0) * ncollSum) + 1
@@ -428,2 +428,2 @@
-         X = ncollNZ(rndIndex,1)+ (pyr(0)-0.5) * dx
-         Y = ncollNZ(rndIndex,2)+ (pyr(0)-0.5) * dy
+         X = ncollpDist(rndIndex,1)+ (pyr(0)-0.5) * dx
+         Y = ncollpDist(rndIndex,2)+ (pyr(0)-0.5) * dy
